    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174458/assistant-professor-of-theater/job": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theater",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Theater Job Number 174458 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division Emory College Department ECAS: Theater Studies Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Campus-Clifton Corridor Required Documents Cover letter, List of References Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description ****DO NOT APPLY HERE**** +++ To learn more about this position and to apply, please visit https://apply.interfolio.com/192989 +++ Emory University Department of Theater and Dance Theater Studies Program Assistant Professor of Acting (tenure-track) The Theater Studies program at Emory University seeks an Assistant Professor of Theater, tenure-track, with a specialization in Acting. The position begins August 1, 2027 and carries a 2-2 teaching load. Successful candidates for the position will demonstrate experience teaching acting courses at the university level alongside a strong record of impactful creative work in performance. The applicant hired will have expertise teaching Acting for the Camera, Acting Fundamentals, and Advanced Scene Study. We also welcome individuals with experience in Stage Combat, Movement, and Audition Techniques. Additional responsibilities will include advising undergraduate thesis projects, curriculum development, committee service, and mentorship of undergraduate students. Candidates may also direct as part of the production season. Candidates must hold a terminal degree which may include an MFA in Acting or an MFA in Directing/ PhD in Theater with substantial experience teaching acting at the university level. Review of Applications will begin November 15, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please address any questions to Theater Studies Chair Noe Montez (noe.montez@emory.edu). All applications are submitted via Interfolio, at https://apply.interfolio.com/192989 . Applicants should upload: cover letter, CV, and the names and contact information of three references that can speak to the candidate’s research and teaching record. Additional materials will be solicited at later stages of the search process. Cover letters should detail areas of research expertise, record of teaching, and candidate’s commitment to supporting students. NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. ****DO NOT APPLY HERE**** Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174403/open-rank--assistant-or-associate-teaching-professor%2c-teaching-track/job": {
      "title": "Open Rank- Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor, Teaching Track",
      "description": "Open Rank- Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor, Teaching Track Job Number 174403 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division Emory College Department ECAS: College Writing Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Campus-Clifton Corridor Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description **PLEASE DO NOT APPLY ON iCIMS. ALL INTERESTED CANDIDATES SHOULD APPLY THROUGH INTERFOLIO: https://apply.interfolio.com/193277** The Writing Program in the Emory College of Arts & Sciences (Atlanta, GA) is accepting applications for an at the rank of Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor in the Emory Writing Program starting in Fall 2027; anticipated start date for this position is August 01, 2027. We seek colleagues with preferred specialization in Composition, Rhetoric, and Writing to join our Writing Program’s interdisciplinary team of teaching-track faculty. We welcome collaborative, innovative administrators and instructors who will complement our strengths in inclusive pedagogy, cultural rhetorics, community-based writing, digital humanities, and writing with quantitative data. The successful candidate will be prepared immediately to serve as the Director of First-Year Writing (FYW). As such, we seek candidates with expertise in first-year composition pedagogy and related research and assessment experience. First-year writing serves about half of the Emory undergraduate student body (~800 students/year) and the director’s responsibilities include training and mentoring instructors at all levels, supporting prospective and enrolled students, developing and assessing curriculum, and running continuing education for writing instructors. While serving as Director of First-Year Writing, they will also collaborate with faculty in the Writing Program to develop and teach a writing pedagogy practicum for graduate student instructors. Additional Information The Emory Writing Program, housed in the Department of English, offers a minor in Rhetoric, Writing, and Information Design (RWID) and has an integrated English Language Learners (ELL) program. We support students in the College of Arts and Sciences and beyond in our long-standing Writing Center. We provide training and support to faculty through WAC/WID initiatives. Our Technical Writing Program reaches students across eighteen departments in the sciences, social sciences, and humanities. Our new faculty member will teach courses like First-Year Writing, Technical Communication, existing courses in the RWID minor, and those developed from their own expertise. Successful applicants will join a highly collaborative team of approximately twenty teaching-track faculty, administrative staff members, and postdoctoral fellows. Members of our program are researchers, writers, and educators who contribute to multidisciplinary and multicultural communities across campus and beyond. Emory’s Atlanta campus is located on the ancestral homeland of the Muscogee (Creek) Nation. In recognition of responsibility to the Muscogee (Creek) Nation, as well as of the historical relationship of the Cherokee Nation to the US Southeast, Emory’s Native American and Indigenous Studies Initiative seeks to “make Indigeneity part of the way Emory does things, in every respect.” The successful candidate for this position will have the chance to join Emory’s robust interdisciplinary communities across campus, including the Departments of African American Studies and the Institute of African Studies, Department of data and Decision Sciences, the Native American and Indigenous Studies Program, the Asian American and Asian Diaspora Studies Initiative, Middle Eastern and South Asian Studies, Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies, the Latin American, Latinx, and Caribbean Studies Program, the Linguistics Program, and the Institute for the Liberal Arts. Teaching-track appointments at Emory are career positions with multi-year contracts, full faculty benefits, and opportunities for promotion and administrative leadership. The standard course assignment for teaching-track faculty is 3/2, and most writing-intensive courses are capped at 16 students. Faculty in administrative roles typically negotiate a reduced teaching load during their term of administrative appointment. Teaching-track faculty have consistent access to funding and resources for teaching, research, and professional development. The salary is competitive and depends upon qualiﬁcations and experience. Appointment terms for teaching-track faculty are dependent upon rank at time of appointment. Minimum Qualifications PhD specializing in composition and rhetoric, writing studies, or related ﬁeld. Demonstrated expertise in scholarship and pedagogies related to FYW. Leadership experience at the program, department, college, or university level. Experience in writing program administration especially preferred. Experience or interest in teaching, mentorship, and/or research in critical data literacies, technical or quantitative communication, and digital rhetorics. Teaching experience in first-year writing and other levels of university writing. Experience working with faculty and students across disciplinary backgrounds. Experience working with a range of student populations using pedagogical approaches that emphasize inclusion and belonging and cultural responsiveness. Desired Qualifications Experience with accessible pedagogies and practices and/or universal design for learning. Familiarity with the educational needs of students who are multilingual and/or from historically underrepresented groups. Engagement with critical and/or justice-oriented pedagogical and methodological approaches. Experience or interest in community-engaged pedagogies and communication. Application Instructions Applicants should submit the following through Interfolio at https://apply.interfolio.com/193277]: Letter of application addressing your multidisciplinary expertise in first-year writing pedagogy and practice, your teaching experience and philosophy, and your teaching and mentorship of students from a range of backgrounds. Curriculum vitae. Candidates selected for interview will provide a teaching portfolio and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin November 4, 2026, but full consideration will be given to all applications received by the deadline of November ?, 2026. Questions? Contact the Director of the Writing Program and Chair of the Search Committee: Dr. Sarah H. Salter, sarah.h.salter@emory.edu. **PLEASE DO NOT APPLY ON iCIMS. ALL INTERESTED CANDIDATES SHOULD APPLY THROUGH INTERFOLIO: https://apply.interfolio.com/193277** NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174401/tenure-track%2c-assistant-professor-in-korean-studies/job": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor in Korean Studies",
      "description": "Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor in Korean Studies Job Number 174401 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division Emory College Department ECAS: REALC Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Campus-Clifton Corridor Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description ** PLEASE DO NOT APPLY ON iCIMS - ALL INTERESTED CANDIDATES SHOULD APPLY THROUGH INTERFOLIO https://apply.interfolio.com/193692 ** The Department of Russian and East Asian Languages and Cultures (REALC) at Emory University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Korean Studies, which was made possible through the generous support of the Korea Foundation, to begin in Fall 2027. Research field and period are open for this position, and we invite applicants with backgrounds in the humanities and/or humanistic social sciences including, but not limited to, the fields of literature, gender studies, media and cultural studies, religion, history, anthropology, and sociology. The Department is particularly interested in candidates whose scholarship is inter-disciplinary and inter-regional (within East Asia and beyond) to complement a dynamic and multidisciplinary community of scholars within REALC specializing in Korea, China, Japan, and Russia. Applicants must have a PhD in hand by the time of appointment. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active research profile. This position carries a 2-2 teaching load, which will include both survey courses on Korea/East Asia and those informed by the candidate’s research expertise and department’s curricular needs. The candidate is also expected to fully engage in departmental activities and to actively contribute at both the college and university levels. Near native proficiency in both English and Korean is required. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, a letter of application detailing the track record of their research, one recent representative publication or work-in-progress (25 pages maximum), teaching portfolio (teaching statement that specifies mentoring and teaching plans, two sample syllabi [one lower-level undergraduate course and one upper-level undergraduate course informed by their research expertise], and course evaluations [if available]) and three letters of recommendation through https://apply.interfolio.com/193692. Inquiries about the position can be sent to Dr. Hwisang Cho (hwisang.cho@emory.edu), the Chair of the Search Committee. Only candidates who are authorized or who can obtain the necessary visa to work in the USA by the start of appointment should apply. Review of applications will start on November 15 and continue until the position is filled. Candidates with disabilities and/or protected veteran status are encouraged to apply. Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). ** PLEASE DO NOT APPLY ON iCIMS - ALL INTERESTED CANDIDATES SHOULD APPLY THROUGH INTERFOLIO https://apply.interfolio.com/193692 ** NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS 