    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174137/weekend-emergency-radiologist-%28full-time-weekendist%29/job": {
      "title": "Weekend Emergency Radiologist (Full-Time Weekendist)",
      "description": "Weekend Emergency Radiologist (Full-Time Weekendist) Job Number 174137 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division School Of Medicine Department SOM: Rad: Emergency Radiology Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory University Hospital Remote Work Classification Primarily Remote – Monthly Health and Safety Information Position involves clinical patient contact, Working with radioactive materials or devices Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description The Department of Radiology and Imaging Sciences at Emory University School of Medicine is seeking a full-time Weekend Emergency Radiologist to join our growing Emergency and Acute Care Imaging Division. Join the 35+ faculty in the Division of Emergency and Trauma Imaging in the Department of Radiology and Imaging Sciences at Emory University. The division provides clinical services across 7 hospitals 24/7/365, including Georgia’s largest Level 1 trauma center. This position is designed for radiologists who prefer a concentrated weekend-focused schedule while maintaining a full-time academic appointment within a nationally recognized academic health system and Emergency and Trauma Imaging Division. Candidates should have an interest in emergency and acute care imaging, possess strong clinical skills in multiple modalities and organ systems, thrive in a fast-paced emergency and inpatient setting and work well in collaboration with other radiologists. Candidates should be prepared to participate in both clinical and non-clinical divisional activities, including teaching and trainee supervision. Position Highlights Full-time (1.0 FTE) Weekendist position 46 weekends annually = 92 shifts Hours: Saturday and Sunday, 1:00 PM to 11:00 PM Work remotely from home anywhere in the USA except Alaska, Hawaii, and New Jersey. Microsoft Teams used for communication with assistance from 24-hour reading room coordinator. Shifts involve whole-body acute care imaging (ED & Inpatient). Mainly CT, US, and XR. Successful candidates will be staffed in tandem with existing emergency/acute care/community radiologists and an emergency neuroradiologist. Provide remote support to residents who are on weekend call shifts. NEW COMP PACKAGE: Very competitive base salary increases in addition to annual academic incentive bonus, professional development fund, and retirement contribution. Compensation rates reflect newly updated and enhanced compensation rates effective 9/1/2026 with base increases of 80-120k. Fellows completing training in summer 2027 are welcome to apply! Academic Environment Faculty are members of the Emory University School of Medicine and benefit from: Collaborative subspecialty support across all radiology divisions Opportunities to teach residents and fellows Protected academic development opportunities Participation in multidisciplinary conferences and quality initiatives Access to extensive research infrastructure Competitive academic compensation package Comprehensive benefits package including public service loan forgiveness (PSLF) Retirement plans with institutional contributions CME support and professional development funding Robust wellness resources through Emory programs Collegial and supportive faculty culture Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree Completion of an ACGME-accredited Diagnostic Radiology residency or alternative pathway program Fellowship training in Emergency Radiology, Abdominal Imaging, Neuroradiology, Musculoskeletal Imaging, or equivalent subspecialty training preferred Applicants must be ABR Board-certified/eligible and eligible to obtain an unrestricted Georgia medical license. Faculty rank will be commensurate with experience and accomplishments. NOTE: Tasks related to this position can be performed remotely with only occasional visits to an Emory University location. Eastern (EST) time zone business hours may apply. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Emory does not approve as a primary work location in the following states; NJ, AK, and HI, any U.S. Territories or outside of the United States. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174125/assistant-professor-in-biological-anthropology/job": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Biological Anthropology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Biological Anthropology Job Number 174125 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division Emory College Department ECAS: Anthropology Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Campus-Clifton Corridor Remote Work Classification Primarily On Campus Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description *** DO NOT APPLY HERE *** All materials should be submitted online through Interfolio by visiting our application website at https://apply.interfolio.com/192888 . The Department of Anthropology at Emory University in Atlanta, GA, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Biological Anthropology, starting in Fall 2027. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research and teaching bridge evolutionary anthropology, comparative anatomy, and biomechanics to address fundamental questions about human evolution, development, and health, drawing on evidence from both fossil and extant populations. The successful candidate will have expertise in comparative anatomy and functional morphology and a research program investigating the evolutionary and developmental origins of human biological variation and their implications for modern human health. We are particularly interested in candidates who employ virtual anthropology in their research and teaching, including the development and application of innovative imaging, computational, and quantitative methods to investigate morphology, function, and variation. We welcome candidates who integrate computational techniques into their research, including artificial intelligence, machine learning, bioinformatics, and big data analytics, all aimed at addressing complex questions related to human evolution and health. Successful applicants will have a Ph.D., post-doctoral research experience, a record of research productivity, and a commitment to undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring. To apply, please submit the following materials via https://apply.interfolio.com/192888 by November 15, 2026: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Statement of Institutional Fit: A statement describing how the applicant’s scholarship, teaching, mentoring, service, and professional goals align with Emory’s mission and principles Contact information for three references NOTE: Position tasks are generally required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location. Remote work from home day options may be granted at department discretion. Emory reserves the right to change remote work status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174107/faculty-position---open-rank-%7c-teaching-track-professor-in-organic-or-biochemical-biophysical-chemistry/job": {
      "title": "Faculty Position - Open Rank | Teaching-Track Professor in Organic or Biochemical/Biophysical Chemistry",
      "description": "Faculty Position - Open Rank | Teaching-Track Professor in Organic or Biochemical/Biophysical Chemistry Job Number 174107 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division Emory College Department ECAS: Chemistry Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Campus-Clifton Corridor Required Documents Cover letter, List of References Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Working in a laboratory Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description ****DO NOT APPLY HERE**** +++To learn more about this position and to apply, please visit https://apply.interfolio.com/192677 +++ Des cription The Department of Chemistry at Emory University invites applications for a teaching track professor (open rank) position in Organic or Bio chemical/ Biophysical Chemistry to teaching both lecture and /or laboratory courses . The candidate will be appointed as Assistant Teaching Professor, Associate Teaching Professor, or Teach i ng Professor depending on qualifications and years of experience in a similar role. This is a career-track position with full faculty governance r ights and responsibilities , competitive salary and benefits , with potential for r egular term renewal and pro motion through the teaching track ranks . The e xpected start date is in the fall of 2027 . The candidate will join a cohesive group of tenure- (28) and teaching-track (7) faculty who teach in our innovative undergraduate curriculum, Chemistry Unbound ( https://pubs.acs.org/doi/pdf/10.1021/acs.jchemed.8b00585 ) . The candidate will be committed to excelling professionally in a department of supportive colleagues who believe that excellence is achieved both individually and collectively. Our faculty, staff, and students contribute to a thriving community of educators and scholars and seek colleagues who are dedicated to joining us in this mission. Qualifications Min i mu m quali fications: Comp le tion of a Ph .D . degree in or ganic chemistry, biochemistry , or biophysical chemistry is required at the start of the appointment. Preferred Q uali fications: Dem onstrated excellence in teaching undergraduate chemistry lecture and/or laboratory courses Demonstrated commitment to working towards collective goals in a team setting Experience i n evidence-based pedagogy and instruct ional creativity Supervising and collaborating with graduate teaching assistants and undergraduate learning assistants Application Instructions A pplicants must apply online at: https://apply.interfolio.com/192677 Review of applications will begin on Oc tober 15 . T o ensure full consideration, all materials should be received by November 15 . A complete appl ication will include: A cover letter out lining your interest in the position and hi ghli ghting releva nt teaching experience A curriculum vitae C ontact information for three referees A statement (up to 3 pages) of teaching experience, educational method s , mentoring experience, and future professional goals For technical assistance with Interfolio , contact help@interfolio.com or call (877) 977-8807. For questions about the position, contact chemsearch@emory.edu . NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. * DO NOT APPLY HERE* Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
