    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/173017/department-of-anesthesiology-faculty-position---euhm-surgical-specialties/job": {
      "title": "Department of Anesthesiology Faculty Position - EUHM Surgical Specialties",
      "description": "Department of Anesthesiology Faculty Position - EUHM Surgical Specialties Job Number 173017 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division School Of Medicine Department SOM: Anesthesiology: Admin Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Midtown Required Documents Cover letter, Letter of Interest, List of References Remote Work Classification Onsite Health and Safety Information Position involves clinical patient contact, Working with human blood, body fluids, tissues, or other potentially infectious materials Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description The Department of Anesthesiology at the Emory University School of Medicine is seeking board eligible/board certified anesthesiologists to join our Emory University Hospital Midtown Surgical Specialties team. Staffed exclusively by Emory University School of Medicine faculty, Emory University Hospital Midtown is a tertiary-care medical center in the heart of midtown Atlanta. Our team performs 22,000 anesthetics per year and serves a unique mix of academic and community providers. Emory University Hospital Midtown Maternity Center also has a growing obstetrical service approaching 6,000 deliveries per year. As a member of the faculty, physicians actively engage in the tripartite mission delivering high-quality clinical care, participating in innovative research, and educating medical students, future anesthesiologists and anesthetists. Emory University’s anesthesiology program includes 48 residents and 20 fellows in ACGME programs such as cardiac, critical care, OB and pain medicine. Position Specifics: OR case mix includes general surgery, ENT, orthopedics, gynecologic surgery, urologic surgery, plastic surgery, surgical 