    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/172696/part-time-assistant-golf-coach/job": {
      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Golf Coach",
      "description": "Part-Time Assistant Golf Coach Job Number 172696 Job Type Temporary Part-Time Division Oxford College Department CHL-Personnel Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Oxford Location : Name Oxford College Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description Job Description: Oxford College of Emory University is seeking a dedicated and experienced Part-Time Assistant College Coach to join both our Men’s and Women’s Golf team. This role involves supporting the head coach in fostering a positive, competitive environment while ensuring the health and safety of athletes. The ideal candidate will have prior coaching experience, strong leadership skills, and a passion for student-athlete development. The assistant coach assists the head coach in running a successful varsity program which competes as a National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA) Division III program and as a member of the Georgia Collegiate Athletic Association (GCAA). This mainly includes help recruiting student-athletes, practice and competition coaching, design and implementation of competitive strategies and advising and mentoring our student-athletes. The assistant must understand and promote the mission, goals, values and educational ideals of Oxford College of Emory University. Key Responsibilities: · Ensure the health, safety, and well-being of athletes on and off the field. · Foster a community of healthy competition and sportsmanship among athletes. · Plan and implement effective and engaging practice sessions. · Assist with team management and logistics. · Maintain open communication with athletes, coaches, and staff. Requirements: · Must be experienced in playing/coaching golf. · Ability to pass a driving and criminal background check. · Availability between 2:30pm-6pm (flexible) primarily Tuesday’s and Thursday in addition to some Monday’s and Wednesday’s. · Availability during some weekends for travel. August through April and possibly needed beginning of June for Nationals (TBD). · Availability during pre-season in August-November and during In-Season January-April. · Strong organizational and communication skills. · Ability to work collaboratively with a diverse group of student-athletes and professional staff. Additional Information: Many of our tournaments will take place across states like Georgia, Florida, North Carolina, South Carolina, Alabama, Tennessee, Kentucky. We additionally have our NJCAA National Championship that takes place in Chautauqua, New York. The assistant coach may or may not be required to travel to New York. If they are needed, accommodations are in place per the college for travel purposes which is taken care of by the Head Coach. Our students are primarily academic focused. Although many are here to compete, we also recognize the importance of our student’s time in the classroom. Practice schedules may vary due to this. The head coach will develop a schedule around the students and keep the assistant coach up to date on practice schedules. There also may be times where you will be encouraged to play alongside the student-athletes during practice days. It is important to note maintaining good communication between head and assistant coach. Days you are unavailable need to be noted prior to hire or prior to travel days. We understand this is a part-time and flexible position but want to ensure you are present and able to fulfill the job requirements and duties. This is a part-time position with flexible hours outside of practice and game schedules. If you are passionate about coaching and ready to contribute to a dynamic athletic program, we encourage you to apply. NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/172694/%c2%a0part-time-assistant-cheer-dance-coach/job": {
      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Cheer/Dance Coach",
      "description": "Part-Time Assistant Cheer/Dance Coach Job Number 172694 Job Type Temporary Part-Time Division Oxford College Department CHL-Personnel Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Oxford Location : Name Oxford College Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Not Applicable Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description The assistant coach assists the head coach in running a successful varsity cheer program which performs and competes as an emerging sport in the National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA) Division III program and as a member of the Georgia Collegiate Athletic Association (GCAA). This mainly includes recruiting student-athletes, assisting with practices, competition coaching, and mentoring our student-athletes. The assistant must understand and promote the mission, goals, values and educational ideals of Oxford College of Emory University. Job Description Cheer/Dance Assistant Coach - Competition Choreography Assist the Head Coach in developing and administering a competitive NJCAA Competition Cheer/Dance Program in accordance with NJCAA and University regulations. Main areas of responsibility include coaching and developing proper stunting techniques, tumbling and choreography. Monitor student-athletes skill progress and provide feedback and motivation to help them improve their performance. Ensure that all training sessions are conducted in a safe and effective manner. This is a part-time (20 hours a week) position without benefits. NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Additional Details