    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/169940/executive-health-physician---open-rank/job": {
      "title": "Executive Health Physician - Open Rank",
      "description": "Executive Health Physician - Open Rank Job Number 169940 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division The Emory Clinic Department TEC GIM - Executive Health Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Clinic Bldg A Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Position involves clinical patient contact, Working with human blood, body fluids, tissues, or other potentially infectious materials Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description Executive Health Physician Opportunity Atlanta, Georgia Emory Healthcare is seeking an internal medicine physician for an exclusive opportunity with the Emory Executive Health Center. This exciting role is responsible for providing an exceptional clinic experience for patients seeking personalized care. About Emory Executive Health Established in 1995, the Emory Executive Health Center is a state-of-the-art practice that offers comprehensive exams and extensive annual testing to those seeking personalized care. Emory Executive Health Center’s approach to preventive medicine has earned national recognition, including Press Ganey, which ranks the program in the top 1% for patient satisfaction. The practice is based at Emory University Hospital (EUH), which is a 750-bed academic quaternary care facility centrally located on the Emory University campus. EUH is one of the nation's leading hospitals in cardiology, oncology, neurology, advanced surgical and transplant services, and more. Opportunity Highlights Step into a unique clinical role in an established program at a nationally reputable institution. Focus on developing strong relationships with an exclusive patient population in a clinic setting. Become the primary point of care for annual visits, testing and diagnostics, chronic disease management, urgent needs, and support wellness goals. Work collaboratively with more than 70 subspecialty resources to coordinate and streamline care. The ideal candidate will be BC ABIM with experience in collaborative health models and executive physicals, excellent patient satisfaction scores, and an innovation and growth mindset. Candidates with fellowship training in internal medicine subspecialties such as cardiology, endocrinology, infectious disease, nephrology, and rheumatology are encouraged to apply. NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remote is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
    },
    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/169909/faculty-position---open-rank/job": {
      "title": "Faculty Position - Open Rank",
      "description": "Faculty Position - Open Rank Job Number 169909 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division The Emory Clinic Department TEC GIM - Executive Health Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory Clinic Bldg A Remote Work Classification No Remote Health and Safety Information Position involves clinical patient contact, Working with human blood, body fluids, tissues, or other potentially infectious materials Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description Concierge Medicine Physician Opportunity Atlanta, Georgia Join Emory Healthcare’s Premier Concierge Medicine Program Emory Healthcare is seeking an outstanding internal medicine physician to join our new Concierge Medicine program, designed for patients who value exceptional, personalized healthcare. This role offers the unique opportunity to practice medicine in a more connected and individualized way, supported by the clinical excellence and academic resources of one of the nation’s top healthcare systems. Opportunity Highlights Provide care for a select panel of patients with enhanced access and a strong emphasis on relationship-based medicine. Deliver care across a variety of settings—clinic, home, inpatient, and virtual—tailored to the needs and preferences of each patient. Focus on preventive care, chronic disease management, and timely responses to urgent concerns, with the goal of supporting long-term health and well-being. Lead a dedicated care team to ensure clear communication and prompt resolution of both clinical and administrative matters. Collaborate with Emory’s broad network of over 70 medical and surgical subspecialties to provide coordinated, streamlined care. Use advanced tools such as Tytocare for remote patient monitoring and digital assessments. Candidate Criteria Board-certified in internal medicine or a subspecialty board with a minimum of 5 years of post-residency experience. Demonstrated excellence in patient care, with strong satisfaction scores and a commitment to service. Proven ability to work in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment. Interest or experience in concierge or personalized care models is a plus. Fellowship training in an internal medicine subspecialty (e.g., cardiology, endocrinology, infectious disease, nephrology, rheumatology) is welcome but not required. About Emory Concierge Medicine Established in 2025, Emory Concierge Medicine is a key component of Emory’s Specialized Services Line. The program combines the benefits of personalized medicine with the depth and rigor of an academic medical center, delivering care that is responsive, evidence-based, and comprehensive. Located at Emory University Hospital (EUH), a 750-bed quaternary care facility consistently ranked among the nation’s top centers for cardiology, oncology, neurology, surgery, and transplantation. Community Details Atlanta has an overall grade of A and is one of the best places to live in Georgia, the best city for young professionals in America, and one of the healthiest cities in America (Niche). Experience the vibrant city life and peaceful suburban living of Metro Atlanta, with a lower cost of living than many major US cities, and many unique and charming neighborhoods to choose from. There are excellent primary school options and highly competitive colleges and universities. The city offers first-class amenities for everyone, including the world's busiest international airport, incredible dining and shopping options, arts and cultural attractions, and sporting events. Often called “the city in the forest,” Atlanta offers an abundance of outdoor recreation in the gorgeous surrounding scenery. NOTE: Position tasks are required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location; working remotely is not an option. Emory reserves the right to change this status with notice to the employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
