    "https://faculty-emory.icims.com/jobs/174879/division-director-of-breast-imaging/job": {
      "title": "Division Director of Breast Imaging",
      "description": "Division Director of Breast Imaging Job Number 174879 Job Type Regular Full-Time Division School Of Medicine Department SOM: Rad: Breast Imaging Campus Location (For Posting) : Location US-GA-Atlanta Location : Name Emory University Hospital Required Documents Cover letter Remote Work Classification Primarily On Campus Health and Safety Information Position involves clinical patient contact, Working with radioactive materials or devices Discover Your Career at Emory University Emory University is a leading research university that fosters excellence and attracts world-class talent to innovate today and prepare leaders for the future. We welcome candidates who can contribute to the excellence of our academic community. Description Reach New Career Heights at Emory University Become a part of something transformative. Emory University is a premier academic institution that champions clinical excellence, pioneering research, and world-class training. The Department of Radiology and Imaging Sciences is committed to cultivating a healthy, collaborative, and sustainable environment where faculty thrive across all career stages. We invite applications and nominations for a strategic, collaborative leader to serve as Division Director for Breast Imaging. Position Overview The Division Director will provide strategic, clinical, operational, and academic leadership for one of the nation’s largest and most comprehensive breast imaging divisions. The Director will partner with clinical and operational leaders across the enterprise to guide the continued growth of breast imaging and advance access, quality, patient experience, and innovation across the network. The Director will also strengthen multidisciplinary collaboration with the Winship Cancer Institute of Emory University (Georgia’s only NCI-Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center) and champion innovative research and education. About the Division & Enterprise Clinical Network: The Breast Imaging Division comprises 23 subspecialty-trained faculty delivering care across seven Emory Healthcare breast imaging centers, regional ambulatory sites, and the breast imaging center at Grady Health System. Education & Training: Emory Radiology hosts 78 residents and 55 fellows, with the Breast Imaging Division recruiting six fellows annually into one of the country's most sought-after programs. Research & Innovation: Multidisciplinary teams collaborate closely with Winship Cancer Institute, the Emory/Georgia Tech Wallace H. Coulter Department of Biomedical Engineering, and national cancer research consortia to drive imaging innovation, AI translational integration, and clinical trials. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic direction, clinical operational oversight, and quality/safety governance for breast imaging across the Emory Healthcare enterprise and Grady Health System. Oversee breast imaging quality, safety, and regulatory compliance across clinical sites, collaborating with designated site-level Lead Interpreting Physicians (LIPs) to ensure adherence to MQSA/FDA requirements. Support the maintenance of ACR accreditations and Breast Imaging Center of Excellence (BICOE) designations, as applicable, across the clinical network. Recruit, retain, mentor, and promote a diverse cohort of academic faculty, fellows, and residents. Advance multidisciplinary clinical operations and clinical research workflows alongside breast surgical oncology, medical oncology, radiation oncology, and pathology. Champion continuous quality improvement, patient satisfaction, and operational efficiency across distributed clinical sites. Qualifications M.D., D.O., or foreign equivalent with American Board of Radiology (ABR) certification (or equivalent). Completion of a subspecialty fellowship in Breast Imaging. Eligibility for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Georgia. Demonstrated track record of clinical excellence and academic, clinical, or operational leadership. Professional qualifications and leadership experience appropriate for faculty appointment at Emory University School of Medicine. Application Process Interested candidates should submit a curriculum vitae and a letter of interest detailing their leadership philosophy, academic background, and clinical focus. Inquiries and nominations may be directed to the Search Committee Co-Chairs: Hernan Bello (hernanbello@emory.edu) Izabella Barreto (izabella.barreto@emory.edu) NOTE: Position tasks are generally required to be performed in-person at an Emory University location. Remote work from home day options may be granted at department discretion. Emory reserves the right to change remote work status with notice to employee. Additional Details Emory is an equal opportunity employer, and qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status or other characteristics protected by state or federal law. Emory University does not discriminate in admissions, educational programs, or employment, including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. Students, faculty, and staff are assured of participation in university programs and in the use of facilities without such discrimination. Emory University complies with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Era Veteran's Readjustment Assistance Act, and applicable executive orders, federal and state regulations regarding nondiscrimination, equal opportunity, and affirmative action (for protected veterans and individuals with disabilities). Inquiries regarding this policy should be directed to the Emory University Department of Equity and Civil Rights Compliance, 201 Dowman Drive, Administration Building, Atlanta, GA 30322. Telephone: 404-727-9867 (V) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). Emory University is committed to ensuring equal access and providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. To request this document in an alternate format or to seek a reasonable accommodation, please contact the Department of Accessibility Services at accessibility@emory.edu or call 404-727-9877 (Voice) | 404-712-2049 (TDD). We kindly ask that requests be made at least seven business days in advance to allow adequate time for coordination. Options Apply Now Apply Share Email this job to a friend Refer Sorry the Share function is not working properly at this moment. Please refresh the page and try again later. Share on your newsfeed Connect With Us! Not ready to apply? Connect with us for general consideration! Application FAQs Software Powered by ICIMS www.icims.com"
